Error: Jet.FailureMarkRequired: `parse` can fail, so the call is written with `?`
  --> Tests/UI/failures_explicit_policy.jet:11:11
    |
 11 |     rows: parse(path)
    |           ^^^^^
 Why: Every call that can pass a failure up writes `?` so each early exit shows in the text
 Fix: Write `?` after the call, or `?(text)` to add a context frame
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.FailureMarkRequired

Error: Jet.FailureMarkRequired: `load` can fail, so the call is written with `?`
  --> Tests/UI/failures_explicit_policy.jet:18:22
    |
 18 |     first + second + load(path).rows
    |                      ^^^^
 Why: Every call that can pass a failure up writes `?` so each early exit shows in the text
 Fix: Write `?` after the call (`call()?.member`), or `?(text)` to add a context frame
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.FailureMarkRequired
